cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CAIMS in your research, please cite it as below. Note that
  citing the software is not a citation of a peer-reviewed methodology:
  CAIMS scores are heuristic behavioral proxies whose construct validity
  has not yet been established (see research/methodology/disclaimer.md).
title: "CAIMS — Consciousness & Alignment Intelligence Measurement System"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Douki
    given-names: Skander
  - name: "Pixels Trade SA"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pixelstrade-dev/CAIMS-Consciousness-Alignment-Intelligence-Measurement-System"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 2.0.0-alpha
date-released: 2026-08-21
keywords:
  - AI evaluation
  - consciousness proxies
  - LLM-as-judge
  - behavioral indicators
  - alignment
abstract: >-
  CAIMS scores consciousness-related behavioral proxy indicators in LLM
  interactions across five theory-inspired dimensions (cognitive
  integration, task alignment, context fidelity, epistemic quality,
  stability) plus an experimental emotional-tone proxy, using an
  LLM-as-judge pipeline with versioned scoring protocols and full
  provenance recording. Scores are explicit proxies, not measurements of
  consciousness.
